('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','What is the SI base unit for amount of substance?','[{"id":"A","text":"metre"},{"id":"B","text":"kilogram"},{"id":"C","text":"mole"},{"id":"D","text":"second"}]'::jsonb,'C','The SI base unit for amount of substance is the mole (mol).','easy','BIPM SI base units','https://www.bipm.org/en/measurement-units/si-base-units','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','What is the SI base unit for electric current?','[{"id":"A","text":"metre"},{"id":"B","text":"kilogram"},{"id":"C","text":"ampere"},{"id":"D","text":"second"}]'::jsonb,'C','The SI base unit for electric current is the ampere (A).','easy','BIPM SI base units','https://www.bipm.org/en/measurement-units/si-base-units','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','What is the SI base unit for length?','[{"id":"A","text":"kilogram"},{"id":"B","text":"ampere"},{"id":"C","text":"metre"},{"id":"D","text":"second"}]'::jsonb,'C','The SI base unit for length is the metre (m).','easy','BIPM SI base units','https://www.bipm.org/en/measurement-units/si-base-units','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','What is the SI base unit for luminous intensity?','[{"id":"A","text":"candela"},{"id":"B","text":"second"},{"id":"C","text":"metre"},{"id":"D","text":"kilogram"}]'::jsonb,'A','The SI base unit for luminous intensity is the candela (cd).','easy','BIPM SI base units','https://www.bipm.org/en/measurement-units/si-base-units','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','What is the SI base unit for mass?','[{"id":"A","text":"kilogram"},{"id":"B","text":"second"},{"id":"C","text":"metre"},{"id":"D","text":"ampere"}]'::jsonb,'A','The SI base unit for mass is the kilogram (kg).','easy','BIPM SI base units','https://www.bipm.org/en/measurement-units/si-base-units','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','What is the SI base unit for thermodynamic temperature?','[{"id":"A","text":"kelvin"},{"id":"B","text":"second"},{"id":"C","text":"metre"},{"id":"D","text":"kilogram"}]'::jsonb,'A','The SI base unit for thermodynamic temperature is the kelvin (K).','easy','BIPM SI base units','https://www.bipm.org/en/measurement-units/si-base-units','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','What is the SI base unit for time?','[{"id":"A","text":"second"},{"id":"B","text":"metre"},{"id":"C","text":"kilogram"},{"id":"D","text":"ampere"}]'::jsonb,'A','The SI base unit for time is the second (s).','easy','BIPM SI base units','https://www.bipm.org/en/measurement-units/si-base-units','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','Which SI derived unit is used to measure capacitance?','[{"id":"A","text":"tesla"},{"id":"B","text":"hertz"},{"id":"C","text":"joule"},{"id":"D","text":"farad"}]'::jsonb,'D','Capacitance is measured in farad (F) in SI.','medium','BIPM SI concise summary','https://www.bipm.org/documents/20126/41483022/SI-Brochure-9-concise-EN.pdf','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','Which SI derived unit is used to measure electric charge?','[{"id":"A","text":"newton"},{"id":"B","text":"coulomb"},{"id":"C","text":"siemens"},{"id":"D","text":"lumen"}]'::jsonb,'B','Electric charge is measured in coulomb (C) in SI.','medium','BIPM SI concise summary','https://www.bipm.org/documents/20126/41483022/SI-Brochure-9-concise-EN.pdf','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','Which SI derived unit is used to measure electric conductance?','[{"id":"A","text":"coulomb"},{"id":"B","text":"siemens"},{"id":"C","text":"lumen"},{"id":"D","text":"pascal"}]'::jsonb,'B','Electric conductance is measured in siemens (S) in SI.','medium','BIPM SI concise summary','https://www.bipm.org/documents/20126/41483022/SI-Brochure-9-concise-EN.pdf','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','Which SI derived unit is used to measure electric potential difference?','[{"id":"A","text":"volt"},{"id":"B","text":"weber"},{"id":"C","text":"lux"},{"id":"D","text":"pascal"}]'::jsonb,'A','Electric potential difference is measured in volt (V) in SI.','medium','BIPM SI concise summary','https://www.bipm.org/documents/20126/41483022/SI-Brochure-9-concise-EN.pdf','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','Which SI derived unit is used to measure electric resistance?','[{"id":"A","text":"newton"},{"id":"B","text":"watt"},{"id":"C","text":"ohm"},{"id":"D","text":"henry"}]'::jsonb,'C','Electric resistance is measured in ohm (Ω) in SI.','medium','BIPM SI concise summary','https://www.bipm.org/documents/20126/41483022/SI-Brochure-9-concise-EN.pdf','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','Which SI derived unit is used to measure energy?','[{"id":"A","text":"farad"},{"id":"B","text":"tesla"},{"id":"C","text":"lux"},{"id":"D","text":"joule"}]'::jsonb,'D','Energy is measured in joule (J) in SI.','medium','BIPM SI concise summary','https://www.bipm.org/documents/20126/41483022/SI-Brochure-9-concise-EN.pdf','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','Which SI derived unit is used to measure force?','[{"id":"A","text":"henry"},{"id":"B","text":"newton"},{"id":"C","text":"coulomb"},{"id":"D","text":"siemens"}]'::jsonb,'B','Force is measured in newton (N) in SI.','medium','BIPM SI concise summary','https://www.bipm.org/documents/20126/41483022/SI-Brochure-9-concise-EN.pdf','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','Which SI derived unit is used to measure frequency?','[{"id":"A","text":"ohm"},{"id":"B","text":"tesla"},{"id":"C","text":"hertz"},{"id":"D","text":"watt"}]'::jsonb,'C','Frequency is measured in hertz (Hz) in SI.','medium','BIPM SI concise summary','https://www.bipm.org/documents/20126/41483022/SI-Brochure-9-concise-EN.pdf','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','Which SI derived unit is used to measure illuminance?','[{"id":"A","text":"lux"},{"id":"B","text":"joule"},{"id":"C","text":"farad"},{"id":"D","text":"weber"}]'::jsonb,'A','Illuminance is measured in lux (lx) in SI.','medium','BIPM SI concise summary','https://www.bipm.org/documents/20126/41483022/SI-Brochure-9-concise-EN.pdf','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','Which SI derived unit is used to measure inductance?','[{"id":"A","text":"coulomb"},{"id":"B","text":"ohm"},{"id":"C","text":"henry"},{"id":"D","text":"newton"}]'::jsonb,'C','Inductance is measured in henry (H) in SI.','medium','BIPM SI concise summary','https://www.bipm.org/documents/20126/41483022/SI-Brochure-9-concise-EN.pdf','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','Which SI derived unit is used to measure luminous flux?','[{"id":"A","text":"siemens"},{"id":"B","text":"lumen"},{"id":"C","text":"pascal"},{"id":"D","text":"volt"}]'::jsonb,'B','Luminous flux is measured in lumen (lm) in SI.','medium','BIPM SI concise summary','https://www.bipm.org/documents/20126/41483022/SI-Brochure-9-concise-EN.pdf','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','Which SI derived unit is used to measure magnetic flux density?','[{"id":"A","text":"hertz"},{"id":"B","text":"watt"},{"id":"C","text":"farad"},{"id":"D","text":"tesla"}]'::jsonb,'D','Magnetic flux density is measured in tesla (T) in SI.','medium','BIPM SI concise summary','https://www.bipm.org/documents/20126/41483022/SI-Brochure-9-concise-EN.pdf','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','Which SI derived unit is used to measure magnetic flux?','[{"id":"A","text":"weber"},{"id":"B","text":"lux"},{"id":"C","text":"joule"},{"id":"D","text":"volt"}]'::jsonb,'A','Magnetic flux is measured in weber (Wb) in SI.','medium','BIPM SI concise summary','https://www.bipm.org/documents/20126/41483022/SI-Brochure-9-concise-EN.pdf','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','Which SI derived unit is used to measure power?','[{"id":"A","text":"henry"},{"id":"B","text":"hertz"},{"id":"C","text":"watt"},{"id":"D","text":"ohm"}]'::jsonb,'C','Power is measured in watt (W) in SI.','medium','BIPM SI concise summary','https://www.bipm.org/documents/20126/41483022/SI-Brochure-9-concise-EN.pdf','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','Which SI derived unit is used to measure pressure?','[{"id":"A","text":"pascal"},{"id":"B","text":"volt"},{"id":"C","text":"weber"},{"id":"D","text":"lumen"}]'::jsonb,'A','Pressure is measured in pascal (Pa) in SI.','medium','BIPM SI concise summary','https://www.bipm.org/documents/20126/41483022/SI-Brochure-9-concise-EN.pdf','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','Which symbol represents the SI base unit ampere?','[{"id":"A","text":"kg"},{"id":"B","text":"A"},{"id":"C","text":"s"},{"id":"D","text":"m"}]'::jsonb,'B','The SI symbol for ampere is A.','easy','BIPM SI base units','https://www.bipm.org/en/measurement-units/si-base-units','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','Which symbol represents the SI base unit candela?','[{"id":"A","text":"s"},{"id":"B","text":"m"},{"id":"C","text":"kg"},{"id":"D","text":"cd"}]'::jsonb,'D','The SI symbol for candela is cd.','easy','BIPM SI base units','https://www.bipm.org/en/measurement-units/si-base-units','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','Which symbol represents the SI base unit kelvin?','[{"id":"A","text":"s"},{"id":"B","text":"m"},{"id":"C","text":"kg"},{"id":"D","text":"K"}]'::jsonb,'D','The SI symbol for kelvin is K.','easy','BIPM SI base units','https://www.bipm.org/en/measurement-units/si-base-units','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','Which symbol represents the SI base unit kilogram?','[{"id":"A","text":"s"},{"id":"B","text":"m"},{"id":"C","text":"A"},{"id":"D","text":"kg"}]'::jsonb,'D','The SI symbol for kilogram is kg.','easy','BIPM SI base units','https://www.bipm.org/en/measurement-units/si-base-units','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','Which symbol represents the SI base unit metre?','[{"id":"A","text":"A"},{"id":"B","text":"m"},{"id":"C","text":"s"},{"id":"D","text":"kg"}]'::jsonb,'B','The SI symbol for metre is m.','easy','BIPM SI base units','https://www.bipm.org/en/measurement-units/si-base-units','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','Which symbol represents the SI base unit mole?','[{"id":"A","text":"kg"},{"id":"B","text":"mol"},{"id":"C","text":"s"},{"id":"D","text":"m"}]'::jsonb,'B','The SI symbol for mole is mol.','easy','BIPM SI base units','https://www.bipm.org/en/measurement-units/si-base-units','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','04903394-7e23-4154-bcfe-f1b6236ef47a'::uuid,'Measurements & Units','Which symbol represents the SI base unit second?','[{"id":"A","text":"m"},{"id":"B","text":"kg"},{"id":"C","text":"A"},{"id":"D","text":"s"}]'::jsonb,'D','The SI symbol for second is s.','easy','BIPM SI base units','https://www.bipm.org/en/measurement-units/si-base-units','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Choose the correct preposition: I agree ___ your suggestion.','[{"id":"A","text":"with"},{"id":"B","text":"to"},{"id":"C","text":"for"},{"id":"D","text":"from"}]'::jsonb,'A','The standard combination is agree with.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Choose the correct preposition: She listens ___ the radio.','[{"id":"A","text":"at"},{"id":"B","text":"for"},{"id":"C","text":"with"},{"id":"D","text":"to"}]'::jsonb,'D','The standard verb-preposition combination is listen to.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Choose the correct preposition: They are waiting ___ the bus.','[{"id":"A","text":"with"},{"id":"B","text":"of"},{"id":"C","text":"for"},{"id":"D","text":"to"}]'::jsonb,'C','The standard combination is wait for.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Choose the correct pronoun: The teacher spoke to Ada and ___.','[{"id":"A","text":"me"},{"id":"B","text":"I"},{"id":"C","text":"we"},{"id":"D","text":"they"}]'::jsonb,'A','The pronoun is the object of the preposition to, so objective case me is correct.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Choose the correct sentence about one item.','[{"id":"A","text":"One of the books be missing."},{"id":"B","text":"One of the books were missing now."},{"id":"C","text":"One of the books is missing."},{"id":"D","text":"One of the books are missing."}]'::jsonb,'C','The head subject one is singular, so is agrees with it.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Choose the correct sentence for a plural subject.','[{"id":"A","text":"The students is ready."},{"id":"B","text":"The students am ready."},{"id":"C","text":"The students be ready."},{"id":"D","text":"The students are ready."}]'::jsonb,'D','The plural subject students agrees with are.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Choose the correct sentence.','[{"id":"A","text":"She has finished her work."},{"id":"B","text":"She have finished her work."},{"id":"C","text":"She has finish her work."},{"id":"D","text":"She finishing has her work."}]'::jsonb,'A','The present perfect uses has/have plus the past participle.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Choose the correct subject-verb agreement.','[{"id":"A","text":"The boy playing football."},{"id":"B","text":"The boy plays football."},{"id":"C","text":"The boy play football."},{"id":"D","text":"The boys plays football."}]'::jsonb,'B','A singular third-person subject takes plays in the simple present.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Which form is a present perfect question?','[{"id":"A","text":"Did you finished?"},{"id":"B","text":"Do you have finished?"},{"id":"C","text":"Are you finish?"},{"id":"D","text":"Have you finished?"}]'::jsonb,'D','Present perfect questions use have/has plus the past participle.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Which phrase correctly uses for to express duration?','[{"id":"A","text":"for last Monday"},{"id":"B","text":"for yesterday"},{"id":"C","text":"for three years"},{"id":"D","text":"for 2020"}]'::jsonb,'C','For is used for a period or duration.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Which phrase correctly uses since?','[{"id":"A","text":"since three years"},{"id":"B","text":"since two hours"},{"id":"C","text":"since several months"},{"id":"D","text":"since 2020"}]'::jsonb,'D','Since refers to a point in time.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Which pronoun is in the possessive case?','[{"id":"A","text":"who"},{"id":"B","text":"theirs"},{"id":"C","text":"them"},{"id":"D","text":"they"}]'::jsonb,'B','Theirs expresses possession.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Which sentence correctly uses the present perfect?','[{"id":"A","text":"I have lived here since 2021."},{"id":"B","text":"I live here since 2021."},{"id":"C","text":"I am living here since 2021."},{"id":"D","text":"I lived here since 2021 and still do."}]'::jsonb,'A','Present perfect is used for a situation that began in the past and continues to the present.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Which sentence uses yet naturally with the present perfect?','[{"id":"A","text":"I am not finish yet."},{"id":"B","text":"I have finish yesterday."},{"id":"C","text":"I haven''t finished yet."},{"id":"D","text":"I didn''t finished yet."}]'::jsonb,'C','Yet commonly appears in present-perfect negatives and questions.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Which tense is most suitable for a completed action at a definite past time such as yesterday?','[{"id":"A","text":"Present continuous"},{"id":"B","text":"Past simple"},{"id":"C","text":"Present perfect"},{"id":"D","text":"Future perfect"}]'::jsonb,'B','Past simple is normally used for a definite completed past time.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','32929c31-b38c-4e52-8214-b656cca924b0'::uuid,'Business Finance','A vehicle used to operate a business and not held for sale is normally what type of asset?','[{"id":"A","text":"Dividend"},{"id":"B","text":"Noncurrent/fixed asset"},{"id":"C","text":"Current liability"},{"id":"D","text":"Revenue item"}]'::jsonb,'B','Operational vehicles are generally fixed/noncurrent assets.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','32929c31-b38c-4e52-8214-b656cca924b0'::uuid,'Business Finance','After liabilities are deducted from assets, the remaining owners'' interest is called what?','[{"id":"A","text":"Equity"},{"id":"B","text":"Revenue"},{"id":"C","text":"Inventory"},{"id":"D","text":"Gross sales"}]'::jsonb,'A','Equity is the residual interest after liabilities.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','32929c31-b38c-4e52-8214-b656cca924b0'::uuid,'Business Finance','For a business, cash is generally classified as what?','[{"id":"A","text":"An expense only"},{"id":"B","text":"A dividend"},{"id":"C","text":"An asset"},{"id":"D","text":"A liability"}]'::jsonb,'C','Cash is an asset.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','32929c31-b38c-4e52-8214-b656cca924b0'::uuid,'Business Finance','For a trading business, unsold inventory is normally classified as what?','[{"id":"A","text":"A dividend"},{"id":"B","text":"A tax"},{"id":"C","text":"An asset"},{"id":"D","text":"A liability"}]'::jsonb,'C','Inventory is an asset.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','32929c31-b38c-4e52-8214-b656cca924b0'::uuid,'Business Finance','In business finance, which equation must a balance sheet satisfy?','[{"id":"A","text":"Assets = Revenue - Expenses"},{"id":"B","text":"Liabilities = Cash + Sales"},{"id":"C","text":"Assets = Liabilities + Shareholders'' Equity"},{"id":"D","text":"Revenue = Assets + Cash"}]'::jsonb,'C','A balance sheet follows Assets = Liabilities + Shareholders'' Equity.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
