('jamb','7b884a45-4327-4631-8b62-0679b6e3f25d'::uuid,'Money & Banking','Why does a central bank pursue price stability?','[{"id":"A","text":"To replace commercial law"},{"id":"B","text":"To support stable economic conditions and preserve money''s value"},{"id":"C","text":"To fix all wages permanently"},{"id":"D","text":"To abolish taxes"}]'::jsonb,'B','Price stability is a central monetary-policy objective that supports stable economic activity.','medium','Central Bank of Nigeria','https://www.cbn.gov.ng/MonetaryPolicy/decisions.html','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','93755e0f-6fbf-403a-b463-c736c0e3971b'::uuid,'Crop & Livestock Management','A key purpose of clean water in livestock management is to support:','[{"id":"A","text":"Seed dormancy"},{"id":"B","text":"Health, growth and reproduction"},{"id":"C","text":"Rusting of equipment"},{"id":"D","text":"Soil erosion"}]'::jsonb,'B','Good feed and clean water are essential for healthy livestock growth and reproduction.','medium','FAO agricultural references','https://www.fao.org/conservation-agriculture/in-practice/species-diversification/en/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','93755e0f-6fbf-403a-b463-c736c0e3971b'::uuid,'Crop & Livestock Management','Crop rotation can help plants explore different soil layers because different crops have:','[{"id":"A","text":"No roots"},{"id":"B","text":"Only surface roots"},{"id":"C","text":"Different rooting depths"},{"id":"D","text":"Identical root systems"}]'::jsonb,'C','FAO explains that different rooting depths allow crops to explore different soil layers.','medium','FAO agricultural references','https://www.fao.org/conservation-agriculture/in-practice/species-diversification/en/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','93755e0f-6fbf-403a-b463-c736c0e3971b'::uuid,'Crop & Livestock Management','Leguminous crops can contribute to soil fertility mainly through:','[{"id":"A","text":"Stopping root growth"},{"id":"B","text":"Biological nitrogen fixation"},{"id":"C","text":"Removing all soil nitrogen"},{"id":"D","text":"Increasing soil salinity"}]'::jsonb,'B','FAO notes that legumes in rotations can add nitrogen through biological fixation.','medium','FAO agricultural references','https://www.fao.org/conservation-agriculture/in-practice/species-diversification/en/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','93755e0f-6fbf-403a-b463-c736c0e3971b'::uuid,'Crop & Livestock Management','Which animal is NOT a ruminant?','[{"id":"A","text":"Chicken"},{"id":"B","text":"Goat"},{"id":"C","text":"Sheep"},{"id":"D","text":"Cattle"}]'::jsonb,'A','Chickens are not ruminants; cattle, sheep and goats are.','medium','FAO agricultural references','https://www.fao.org/conservation-agriculture/in-practice/species-diversification/en/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','93755e0f-6fbf-403a-b463-c736c0e3971b'::uuid,'Crop & Livestock Management','Which combination lists nutrients animals require in their feed?','[{"id":"A","text":"Only water and salt"},{"id":"B","text":"Only protein"},{"id":"C","text":"Only carbohydrates"},{"id":"D","text":"Carbohydrates, proteins, fats, vitamins and minerals"}]'::jsonb,'D','FAO lists carbohydrates, proteins, fats, vitamins and minerals among required feed nutrients.','medium','FAO agricultural references','https://www.fao.org/conservation-agriculture/in-practice/species-diversification/en/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','93755e0f-6fbf-403a-b463-c736c0e3971b'::uuid,'Crop & Livestock Management','Which group contains only common ruminant livestock?','[{"id":"A","text":"Pigs, rabbits and poultry"},{"id":"B","text":"Cattle, sheep and goats"},{"id":"C","text":"Pigs, chickens and rabbits"},{"id":"D","text":"Chickens, ducks and turkeys"}]'::jsonb,'B','FAO identifies cattle, sheep and goats as ruminant livestock.','medium','FAO agricultural references','https://www.fao.org/conservation-agriculture/in-practice/species-diversification/en/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','93755e0f-6fbf-403a-b463-c736c0e3971b'::uuid,'Crop & Livestock Management','Which nutrient group is a major source of energy in animal feed?','[{"id":"A","text":"Minerals only"},{"id":"B","text":"Water only"},{"id":"C","text":"Vitamins only"},{"id":"D","text":"Carbohydrates"}]'::jsonb,'D','Carbohydrates are an important energy source in feed.','medium','FAO agricultural references','https://www.fao.org/conservation-agriculture/in-practice/species-diversification/en/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','93755e0f-6fbf-403a-b463-c736c0e3971b'::uuid,'Crop & Livestock Management','Which nutrient is especially important as a building material for muscles in animals?','[{"id":"A","text":"Water only"},{"id":"B","text":"Ash"},{"id":"C","text":"Carbon dioxide"},{"id":"D","text":"Protein"}]'::jsonb,'D','FAO animal-health guidance describes protein as a building block needed for muscles.','medium','FAO agricultural references','https://www.fao.org/conservation-agriculture/in-practice/species-diversification/en/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','93755e0f-6fbf-403a-b463-c736c0e3971b'::uuid,'Crop & Livestock Management','Which of the following is a major benefit of crop rotation?','[{"id":"A","text":"Elimination of water needs"},{"id":"B","text":"Prevention of every plant disease"},{"id":"C","text":"Improved nutrient use and reduced pest risk"},{"id":"D","text":"Permanent removal of all soil organisms"}]'::jsonb,'C','Crop rotation can improve nutrient use and reduce pest and weed risks.','medium','FAO agricultural references','https://www.fao.org/conservation-agriculture/in-practice/species-diversification/en/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','93755e0f-6fbf-403a-b463-c736c0e3971b'::uuid,'Crop & Livestock Management','Which practice can improve the diversity of soil flora and fauna?','[{"id":"A","text":"Rotating different crop species"},{"id":"B","text":"Growing only one crop continuously"},{"id":"C","text":"Removing all crop residues"},{"id":"D","text":"Eliminating all roots"}]'::jsonb,'A','FAO notes that crop diversity in rotation supports diverse soil flora and fauna.','medium','FAO agricultural references','https://www.fao.org/conservation-agriculture/in-practice/species-diversification/en/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','93755e0f-6fbf-403a-b463-c736c0e3971b'::uuid,'Crop & Livestock Management','Which practice helps reduce the carry-over of crop-specific pests and diseases?','[{"id":"A","text":"Overgrazing"},{"id":"B","text":"Bush burning"},{"id":"C","text":"Crop rotation"},{"id":"D","text":"Continuous monocropping"}]'::jsonb,'C','FAO notes that crop rotation helps prevent carry-over of crop-specific pests and diseases.','medium','FAO agricultural references','https://www.fao.org/conservation-agriculture/in-practice/species-diversification/en/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('jamb','93755e0f-6fbf-403a-b463-c736c0e3971b'::uuid,'Crop & Livestock Management','Which three nutrients are commonly referred to as NPK fertilizer nutrients?','[{"id":"A","text":"Nitrogen, phosphorus and potassium"},{"id":"B","text":"Nitrogen, protein and potassium"},{"id":"C","text":"Nitrate, phosphate and kerosene"},{"id":"D","text":"Nickel, phosphorus and krypton"}]'::jsonb,'A','NPK refers to nitrogen, phosphorus and potassium.','medium','FAO agricultural references','https://www.fao.org/conservation-agriculture/in-practice/species-diversification/en/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
